# File: client/.env.example
# Purpose: Public API base URL used by the client build.
# Responsibility: Shared frontend development.
#
# Implementation guide.
#
# Integration contract:
# Public variable: VITE_API_URL. Values are part of the built browser bundle. There are no
# actual environment assignments in this ZIP.
#
# Acceptance criteria:
# A teammate can point the client to either local Express or the deployed backend without
# editing React pages.
#
# Implementation steps:
# 1. After reading the guide, write VITE_API_URL with a local example value of
#    http://localhost:4000/api.
# 2. Copy the implemented template to client/.env locally and keep the real local file out of
#    Git.
# 3. On Vercel set VITE_API_URL to https://your-service.onrender.com/api before building. A
#    changed Vite environment value requires a new frontend build.
# 4. The base URL already includes /api. API wrapper paths start with /auth, /quizzes,
#    /attempts, or /results; they must not append another /api.
# 5. Only put public settings in VITE_ variables. JWT_SECRET, database paths, passwords, and
#    private keys belong exclusively to the server.
# 6. Match server CLIENT_ORIGIN to the resulting Vercel origin. This file does not configure
#    server CORS.
#
# Related files and dependencies:
# client/src/api/http.js
# client/vite.config.js
# server/.env.example
